    {
      "id": "agent-orchestrator",
      "name": "Agent Orchestrator",
      "description": "Real parallel multi-agent orchestration for KiroCrew: an orchestrator session divides a goal into items, runs one worker session per item at the same time, and coordinates them live over a typed, bounded message bus (hub-and-spoke: every worker reports to the orchestrator, which relays; worker ⇄ worker is an opt-in setting) with wake-ups, a wait-any primitive and per-worker status lines. Ships the `agent-orchestrator` and `agent-orchestrator-worker` agents (built on the host's session-control and work-ledger tools, which stay untouched) and a live hub-and-spoke graph page with an animated message bus. Unofficial.",
